vation. Thirdly, **Cost Efficiency:** Custom silicon allows them to cut costs in specific ways and to sell $500 boxes that rival $1500 PCs. Generic, standardized parts would be more expensive for the same performance. And finally, to address the core idea – the user is essentially describing the PC! It is the standardized platform where everything compiles the same way, but it is not a closed ecosystem. In the end, it’s a mix of capitalist competition and the desire to build unique hardware experiences that keep the platforms separate. Great question! It really gets to the heart of how this industry operates.
